  "description": "A 45-degree wye with a small lateral (beta^2 = 0.16) whose flow split has no self-consistent value: the Crane TP-410 lateral K jumps up at a split of 0.4, and the network gives a split above 0.4 with the formula below it and below 0.4 with the formula above it. Verifies the step hold: K held at the mean of the fluids values at the two splits the outer iteration alternates between, the flows that K gives, and the CORRELATION_OUT_OF_RANGE flag on the wye.",
  "source": "closed-form: tests/reference/derivations_branches.py::wye_crane_step_hold (Darcy-Weisbach + Colebrook lines; fluids K_branch_diverging_Crane and K_run_diverging_Crane at angle 45; splits of the outer update with K linearized about the last split (central difference on its side of the step), iterated to its 2-cycle across q = 0.4; path K held at the mean of the fluids values at the two splits (design 5.4); fsolve; line fittings: fluids entrance_sharp(method='Crane'), exit_normal())",
